@host = http://localhost:5247
@reportCode = N8v2dBGMZX6wrfaA
@fightId = 106
@sourceId = 7
@playerName = REPLACE_PLAYER

# These requests call the application API; none accepts an edition parameter.
# Seasons, rankings and report summary are existing static/sample responses.
# Rankings accepts optional season (default "current").
# Lookup and analysis require configured WCL credentials and consume upstream quota.
# Replace fightId/sourceId/playerName with identities visible in the selected report.
# Lookup: 200, 400, 429, 500. The report code is trimmed before the WCL call.
# Lookup returns report startTime, zone, and fights with encounterID, kill,
# difficulty, startTime and endTime for the manual Reports page.
# Analysis: 200, 400, 404, 429, 500. Errors contain "error"; 500 also includes "detail".
# Analysis requires reportCode. Optional fightId/sourceId/playerName select the subject;
# omitted selections use the service's default fight/actor resolution.
# Optional parsePercentile and itemLevel affect scoring; eventLimit defaults to 5000
# and is clamped to 100-10000 by the service.

### Static season listing
GET {{host}}/api/warcraftlogs/seasons
Accept: application/json

### Sample rankings with default season
GET {{host}}/api/warcraftlogs/rankings
Accept: application/json

### Sample rankings with selected season
GET {{host}}/api/warcraftlogs/rankings?season=season-1
Accept: application/json

### Sample report summary; this is NOT the live metadata lookup
GET {{host}}/api/warcraftlogs/reports/{{reportCode}}
Accept: application/json

### Live report metadata
GET {{host}}/api/warcraftlogs/reports/{{reportCode}}/lookup
Accept: application/json

### Analyze by actor ID with every supported body field
POST {{host}}/api/warcraftlogs/rotation/analyze
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reportCode": "{{reportCode}}",
  "fightId": {{fightId}},
  "sourceId": {{sourceId}},
  "playerName": "{{playerName}}",
  "parsePercentile": 95,
  "itemLevel": 490,
  "eventLimit": 5000
}

### Analyze by player name instead of actor ID
POST {{host}}/api/warcraftlogs/rotation/analyze
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reportCode": "{{reportCode}}",
  "fightId": {{fightId}},
  "playerName": "{{playerName}}"
}

### Minimal analysis using default subject resolution
POST {{host}}/api/warcraftlogs/rotation/analyze
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reportCode": "{{reportCode}}"
}

### Blank report code: 400 without an upstream call
POST {{host}}/api/warcraftlogs/rotation/analyze
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reportCode": " "
}

### Missing required reportCode property: 400 during body binding
POST {{host}}/api/warcraftlogs/rotation/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{}
